  "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {3}^{1-5x}+6 & >0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {3}^{1-5x} & >-6 \\\\ {3}^{1-5x} & >-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause a power of a positive number is always greater than $0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{3}^{1-5x}>0\n$$\n\nfor all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the inequality ${3}^{1-5x}>-10$ is satisfied for all real values of $x.$",
